direction: right
title: |md
  # From application to credit score
| {near: top-center}

input: |md
  **Loan application**

  income, credit history,

  loan amount, rate,

  purpose, credit profile
| {shape: rectangle; class: actor}
bin: |md
  **Attributes**

  each value falls

  into a fitted bin

  or category
| {shape: rectangle; class: box}
woe: |md
  **Weight of Evidence**

  ln(good share ÷

  bad share)

  per attribute
| {shape: rectangle; class: box}
model: |md
  **Logistic regression**

  ln(odds) = intercept +

  Σ coefficient × WOE
| {shape: rectangle; class: key}
pd: |md
  **Probability of default**

  1 ÷ (1 + e^−ln(odds))

  example: 5.4%
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
score: |md
  **Credit score and grade**

  Offset − Factor × ln(odds)

  example: 569.55, grade BB
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
points: |md
  **Score attribution**

  base 562 + points

  per characteristic
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
input -> bin
bin -> woe
woe -> model
model -> pd
model -> score
model -> points
